From: gvwifi-los23 build kit
Subject: [PATCH] hwc2on1adapter: allow devices to declare HWC1 retire fences reliable

The adapter unconditionally advertises PresentFenceIsNotReliable, which makes
SurfaceFlinger keep HW vsync enabled forever. On the SM-T670 (Exynos 7580,
s3c_fb/decon) the retire fence is signaled only after vsync once the shadow
registers latched the new frame, i.e. a correct present fence. Measured
before: SurfaceFlinger ~64% CPU during 1080p video with HW vsync always on.
Opt-in via ro.vendor.hwc.present_fence_reliable=true; default unchanged.

---
diff --git a/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp b/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp
index f14cbc7..49b9f8b 100644
--- a/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp
+++ b/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include <sstream>
 #include <type_traits>
 
+#include <cutils/properties.h>
 #include <hardware/hwcomposer.h>
 #include <log/log.h>
 #include <utils/Trace.h>
@@ -2270,8 +2271,15 @@ void HWC2On1Adapter::populateCapabilities() {
 
     // Some devices might have HWC1 retire fences that accurately emulate
     // HWC2 present fences when they are deferred, but it's not very reliable.
-    // To be safe, we indicate PresentFenceIsNotReliable for all HWC1 devices.
-    mCapabilities.insert(Capability::PresentFenceIsNotReliable);
+    // To be safe, we indicate PresentFenceIsNotReliable for all HWC1 devices,
+    // unless the device declares that its retire fences are signaled at the
+    // vsync where the frame starts scanning out (e.g. Exynos s3c_fb/decon,
+    // which signals only after the shadow registers have latched).
+    if (property_get_bool("ro.vendor.hwc.present_fence_reliable", false)) {
+        ALOGI("HWC1 retire fences declared reliable; exposing present fences");
+    } else {
+        mCapabilities.insert(Capability::PresentFenceIsNotReliable);
+    }
 }
 
 HWC2On1Adapter::Display* HWC2On1Adapter::getDisplay(hwc2_display_t id) {
